course: dictionary
lesson: 533
title: Small word, big jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «at» is tiny, but it does many jobs. It can show where something is, when it happens, what you look towards, or how well you do something. The words next to «at» tell you which job it is doing.
explain: Place and time: «at the shop» shows where, and «at night» shows when. «Inside the Arctic and Antarctic Circles, there is at least one day a year when the Sun does not set.» Here «at least» means not less than, so the sentence says one day or more.
explain: Aim and skill: «A boy in Halifax squints at the board» shows what he is looking towards. «Good at maths» shows how well someone does maths. Prices work the same way: «at 2 dollars each» tells you the cost of one thing.
explain: Watch out for the same word in other places. In an email address, the «@» sign is called the at sign. In everyday talk you might hear «Where are you at?», which asks how far you have got. When you are not sure, look at the words around it and try a meaning in the sentence.
fact: At is a preposition. It shows place, time, direction, rate or skill.
fact: «At the shop» means in or near the shop. It tells you where.
fact: «At noon» and «at the start» tell you when something happens.
fact: «Look at the board» means to turn your eyes towards the board.
fact: «@» is the at sign, used in email addresses and online names.
exercise: She is good ___ maths. Which small word fits the gap? | in | on | with | *at
exercise: «A boy in Halifax squints at the board and sits closer and closer.» What does at show here? | How tall he is | The price of the board | The time of day | *What he is looking towards
exercise: The pens are sold at 2 dollars each. What does at show? | A feeling | *A price | A place | A time
exercise: test
test: In «at least one day a year», what does at least mean? | *Not less than | Next to a river | Very sad | Before lunch
test: In an email address like name@school.org, what is the @ sign called? | The hash | The slash | *The at sign | The dot
exam: In the formal phrase «at a unit cost of», what is at showing? | A time | A feeling | *A price or rate | A place
